WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.602
The VAC disability benefits backlog doubled in a single year — from five thousand six hundred to over eleven thousand.

00:00:06.602 --> 00:00:11.034
Only forty-seven percent of applications meet the sixteen-week standard.

00:00:11.034 --> 00:00:17.897
Thirty-one percent of newly released members access zero VAC services in the critical first year after leaving the military.

00:00:17.897 --> 00:00:22.443
Seven hundred and fifty dollars per month — that is the VAC Housing Benefit.

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:25.784
It is below market rent in every major Canadian city.

00:00:25.784 --> 00:00:34.454
A ninety-two percent increase in disability benefit applications between 2015 and 2025, but the system was never scaled to match.

00:00:34.454 --> 00:00:38.977
Six-month-plus delays at seven of eleven Operational Stress Injury clinics.

00:00:38.977 --> 00:00:46.295
Billions in unspent VAC funding lapsed annually — the money was allocated by Parliament, then not delivered to veterans.

00:00:46.295 --> 00:00:48.545
The government does not lack resources.

00:00:48.545 --> 00:00:51.249
It lacks the will to spend them on the people who served.
